# Canonical author identity.
#
# Ninety-one early commits were authored from personal mailboxes before the
# repository was public. `user.email` is the GitHub noreply address now, so
# nothing new arrives under any other name — this maps what already landed.
#
# ⚠️ A mailmap changes what git DISPLAYS, not what the commits contain. Every
# tool that reads it — `git log`, `git shortlog`, `git blame`, most CI and
# release tooling — shows the canonical address. The GitHub web UI does not
# read it, so the original addresses stay visible on those commits there.
# Removing them from a public repository means rewriting history and
# force-pushing 5,800+ commits, which was considered and declined.
